WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.446 --> 00:00:14.916
Marcus Bell: Hey Priyanka, hey Carla. How's it going? You're on the road, Carla? I hear some background noise.

2
00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:23.162
Carla Nguyen: Yeah, sorry, I'm in the truck. Just left the the Pineville branch. Give me one sec, let me pull over. Okay.

3
00:00:23.162 --> 00:00:23.837
Carla Nguyen: Hi Marcus.

4
00:00:24.888 --> 00:00:30.453
Priyanka Shah: Hi Marcus. Sorry we're a couple minutes late. Carla had to run something over to dispatch.

5
00:00:31.315 --> 00:00:36.323
Marcus Bell: Uh, no worries at all. How's the the start of the week looking?

6
00:00:36.684 --> 00:00:45.380
Priyanka Shah: Busy. We're seeing the usual fall HVAC rush. Last week we we had, I I think, 4,100 calls total across like, all 14 branches.

7
00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:49.004
Priyanka Shah: Around 2,600 were HVAC, rest split between plumbing and electrical.

8
00:00:49.212 --> 00:00:58.375
Carla Nguyen: Feels like more, honestly. We had two dispatchers out with that stomach thing, so the board was a mess Thursday and Friday.

9
00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:00.394
Marcus Bell: Ugh. Are they back?

10
00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:04.212
Carla Nguyen: One's back today. The other, Wednesday. We're limping along.

11
00:01:04.982 --> 00:01:17.702
Marcus Bell: Okay. So what I wanted to do today, quick check-in. Anything on your list. I know PreSense went live in June, um, so I want to hear how that's I mean, sitting with the branches.

12
00:01:17.702 --> 00:01:20.246
Marcus Bell: And then anything on the tracking side.

13
00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:29.064
Priyanka Shah: PreSense is good. The agents like seeing the ad and the pages before they pick up. We haven't had any complaints there.

14
00:01:29.064 --> 00:01:34.807
Priyanka Shah: Google Ads side is fine too, the offline conversions are flowing, Smart Bidding's been steady.

15
00:01:35.022 --> 00:01:37.874
Carla Nguyen: Yeah, that part's fine. It's the spam thing.

16
00:01:38.075 --> 00:01:39.812
Marcus Bell: I mean, the spam signals.

17
00:01:40.305 --> 00:01:56.998
Carla Nguyen: So here's what's happening. Our after-hours line, right? People call at like 10:30 at night, or Saturday morning, because their AC died or a water heater's leaking. And Signal AI is tagging a bunch of those as spam.

18
00:01:56.998 --> 00:02:00.073
Carla Nguyen: So they drop out of the reporting.

19
00:02:00.426 --> 00:02:04.334
Marcus Bell: Okay. So real customers, calling after hours, getting flagged.

20
00:02:05.265 --> 00:02:15.216
Carla Nguyen: Real customers. I had one Saturday, guy called at 11:40 p.m. about a burst pipe, we booked him, tech went out at 6 a.m.

21
00:02:15.216 --> 00:02:24.337
Carla Nguyen: Sunday. And in the report that call is spam. So as far as the report is concerned we never got that call.

22
00:02:25.525 --> 00:02:38.014
Priyanka Shah: And And it's not just one. I pulled last month, and I'd say there were, I don't know, 60, 70 calls flagged that way that had actual booked appointments attached.

23
00:02:38.014 --> 00:02:39.679
Priyanka Shah: Mostly nights and weekends.

24
00:02:40.419 --> 00:02:48.854
Marcus Bell: Got it. And is it the after-hours number specifically, or are you seeing it on the main tracking numbers too?

25
00:02:50.189 --> 00:02:53.719
Priyanka Shah: Mostly the after-hours line. Some on the weekend campaign numbers.

26
00:02:55.026 --> 00:03:01.838
Marcus Bell: Okay. Let me ask a couple things. Are those calls coming in through the the IVR, or ringing straight through?

27
00:03:02.551 --> 00:03:08.622
Carla Nguyen: Straight through, mostly. After 8 p.m. the IVR just forwards to the on-call phone.

28
00:03:09.855 --> 00:03:21.024
Marcus Bell: Uh, that might be part of it, but I don't want to guess. Let me take this back to the Signal AI team, get the call IDs, and see what's tripping the classification.

29
00:03:21.024 --> 00:03:25.086
Marcus Bell: Can you send me, say, five or six examples with the timestamps?

30
00:03:25.742 --> 00:03:30.162
Priyanka Shah: Yeah, I'll pull them and send them over. Today or tomorrow.

31
00:03:31.521 --> 00:03:40.393
Marcus Bell: Perfect. And Priyanka, is this something you've been working around in your reports, or is it just noise at this point?

32
00:03:41.109 --> 00:03:50.807
Priyanka Shah: Workaround. I've been manually checking the recordings for the flags, but that's, you know, an hour or two a week I don't really have.

33
00:03:51.378 --> 00:03:58.265
Marcus Bell: Understood. Okay. Uh, Anything else before I let you two go? I know Carla's double-parked or whatever.

34
00:03:59.173 --> 00:04:06.170
Carla Nguyen: Ha, close. No, that's it from me. Just fix the spam thing so my guys get credit for the midnight calls.

35
00:04:07.257 --> 00:04:10.946
Marcus Bell: Fair. I'll follow up once I hear back. Talk soon, both.

36
00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:13.080
Priyanka Shah: Thanks Marcus. Bye.

37
00:04:13.697 --> 00:04:14.497
Carla Nguyen: Um, Bye.
